A||||2||JohnnyK||Strange problem (printer related)||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||12-06-2000||11:25 PM||||I am trying to print these hoist plans that I got (thanks again) and they are in jpeg format, but it prints half the page and then says "error printing to lpt1 blah blah" and a page shoots out saying the printer has reached its full capacity. I don't want to dilute the resolution or anything (assuming that would work) as it is fairly hard to read now. and I tried changing the fonts to "display fonts as graphics" but that didn't work. Is there anything I can do (besides adding memory to my printer). Can I change it's format to something that would print or something? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||RNGCRSH||12-06-2000||11:41 PM||||In the settings for your printer driver(if its an ink jet), make sure it is not set to print after entire document is spooled, or you will have to have more memory. If its a laser printer then you will have to up the memory or reduce the size of the image.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-07-2000||10:40 PM||||That sounds like a laser printer. Inkjets and dot matrix don't usually have problems like that. You'll have to see about adding RAM to the printer. ||||reg||1
